# Channel Configuration

Copy this file to channel-config.md and fill in your own values.
The tools read lines written as "Key: value". Keys are not case sensitive.
channel-config.md is ignored by git, so your details stay on your computer.

---

## Channel Identity

Channel Name: Your Channel Name
Channel ID: UCxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
Channel Tagline: Your short tagline or series name
Presenter: Your Full Name
Follow Name: Your first name

## Series Settings

Series Name: Your Series Name
Series Badge: YOUR SERIES NAME
Episode Min Minutes: 7
Episode Max Minutes: 10
Host 1 Name: Alex
Host 2 Name: Elena
Presenter Look: the same person as in the reference image

## Follow Links (used in every description and on the end screen)

LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/your-handle
Medium: https://medium.com/@your-handle
X: https://x.com/your-handle
Subscribe link: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx?sub_confirmation=1

## Publish Schedule

Publish slot: Tuesday or Thursday, 9:00 AM your local time
Short beginner content: Tuesday / Thursday / Saturday / Sunday, 8 to 9 PM your local time
Long advanced content: Saturday, 9 to 10 AM your local time

## Links to Never Use (optional, comma separated)

Banned Links: old-handle, wrong-link-fragment

## Episode Numbering

Viewers see the published order (Episode 1, 2, 3 ...), not your folder numbers. Keep a note of the mapping here,
for example: file EP01 = Episode 1, file EP03 = Episode 2.

## Standard Description Layout

1. Hook: two lines with the main search phrase and the promise
2. Short summary paragraph
3. Optional summary in a second language
4. What you will learn
5. Chapters
6. Sources, next episode, series blurb
7. About the channel, subscribe link, follow block
8. Hashtags last, never more than 15
